[ceiling] Functional aft tie tunnel: under the aft Reservoir A paired seat the strap runs through a 3.2 mm transverse slot. This 7.5 × 3.2 mm roof is the seat's ridge between the two tubes, 1.6 mm over the slot floor, and it bridges the slot's 3.2 mm width.
alternatives: An open-topped slot cuts the ridge that carries both tubes' grooves. A sloped roof takes stock from that ridge or deepens the slot into the lid's floor stock.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=19.800 y=90.250 z=5.175

[ceiling] Functional lower B-fill fitting pocket: the flat underside at world Z251.4 clears the fixed lower elbow and retains its 3.05 mm roof to Z254.45. This open-bottom dry pocket receives the fitting before the lid closes. Retain Tree(auto)/Default support decisions; actual support release, retention force and print quality are unqualified.
alternatives: Filling the pocket obstructs the elbow. Changing its ceiling or fitting station requires reconciling the fixed reservoir stem and direct link; the flat pocket preserves those selected interfaces.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=84.119 y=-42.264 z=3.400

[thin] Unavoidable without moving the stack's clamp stations: each clamp screw's Ø3.3 clearance hole stands on the shared attachment station, 4 mm in from the bare outside face at the shell's Ø8 boss centre. The plain casing face reserves 0.30 mm for foil inside the enclosure envelope, leaving 2.04–2.05 mm of wall below the head pocket floor.
alternatives: Moving the stations inboard moves the shell's bosses and every cap's and lid's holes, Derek's printed shell among them. Moving the outside face outward spends the reserved foil allowance. Carrying the head pocket's outward slot down through the plate removes the wall and leaves the screw's floor open to the side.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
