[sliver] Functional fore snap catch: each 0.60 mm-wide underside is the full-Y bearing ledge that captures the cap hook while leaving the outward spring lane open. Its fixed section is 3 mm tall. The cap's hook has 0.45 mm engagement, with separate 0.25 mm sliding side air and 0.40 mm underside allowance. The local dense receiver/root modifier and emitted-path reading describe deposition, not printed retention or surface acceptance.
alternatives: Increasing this projection to 3 mm widens the whole matching cap by 4.8 mm. Filling the space below the ledge blocks the integral hook; removing the ledge removes positive retention. A local relief merely moves those conflicts to a new edge instead of resolving the mating shape.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=114.050 y=64.625 z=8.400
click: x=114.050 y=43.875 z=8.400

[ledge] Functional flat snap bearing underside: these two 6.5 × 0.6 mm faces catch the cap's full-span hooks after outward flex and spring-back. Their flat contact keeps retention from camming the cap outward under withdrawal. Tree(auto)/Default adds no support-interface box within the fore receiver/root region in the current offline lid slice; the 0.40 mm underside allowance remains in the mating geometry. The receiver is open above and at both flanks for inspection and cleanup before the tubes and cap enter.
alternatives: Sloping or rounding away the flat changes the withdrawal catch into a release ramp. A corbel fills the hook's seating space. A 3 mm projection requires a matching cap 4.8 mm wider and changes the approved spring and hook geometry. Support finish and release effort remain physical qualifications.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=115.133 y=43.775 z=8.400
click: x=115.133 y=64.525 z=8.400

[sliver] Functional shallow spring-foot clearance pockets. These 0.65 mm-high sides bound the two flat-bottomed reliefs that let the retained fore cap sit at Z258.5 with 0.25 mm floor clearance. The floors retain 4.75 mm of lid backing; the pockets end at the receiver neck without cutting its 3 mm cheeks. The native seated and spread-cap readings show zero overlap with the lid.
alternatives: Raising the cap and tubes 0.65 mm to clear the uncut lid leaves only 0.735 mm under V-B for the fill tube, below the selected 1 mm buffer. Lowering the whole lid face alters its broad 5.4 mm plate and the roots of the other fixed features. Removing the pockets obstructs the cap; the local relief preserves the selected tube and mating-cap geometry.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
